<title>UK: BNG sets two zero-coupon rand bonds.</title>
<headline>BNG sets two zero-coupon rand bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Nederlandse Gemeenten has issued two rand zero-coupon bonds, lead manager Toronto Dominion said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>One bond is for 2.5 billion rand and matures in December 2017. The other is for four billion rand and matures in December 2020.</p>
<p>* * * *  </p>
<p> AMT    2.5 BLN RAND  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    29.DEC.17</p>
<p> TYPE   ZERO-COUPON   ISS PRICE  6.75	PAY DATE    29.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  40 BP     REOFFER    6.50	SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MGT/UND    15 BP     SELL CONC  25 BP</p>
<p>* * * *  </p>
<p> AMT    4.0 BLN RAND  COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    29.DEC.20</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  4.825     PAY DATE    29.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  37.5 BP   REOFFER    4.575     SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MGT/UND    12.5 BP   SELL CONC  25 BP</p>
<p>* * * *  </p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX/AMST</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS US/UK/SA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    DUTCH     HOME CTRY  N/LANDS   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
